Zanath  posted 06-20-2001 09:35 AM CT (US)      <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Ok all, being a Druid born and bred I am still getting used to Tanking in the world of EQ  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"> I have my warrior up to 26 now and have Good Equipment so far basically a low 40's Tweak. My current dilemma is that I have around 14k I am planning on dumping for my Warrior question is where does it go. Have a WS and a decent off hander so wasn't thinking of weapon my thoughts were more on should I get Haste (FBSS and misc AC), Upgrade AC (Figuring I can get my ac raised by 70) or should I get my str to 200 (and misc AC raised by about 20) anyone have any ideas  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><BR>I was leaning towards AC since I pretty much outdamage anyone in group Tank wise with my weapons so the Haste might make me more of a Target...<P>Thanks for any help all. I just want to make the most informed decision before I regret it.<P>Zanath<BR>Forever the 51 Druid<P>Teijnal<BR>soon to be 51 Warrior  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"> <BR> <BR>Sleethr   posted 06-20-2001 09:49 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Hmmm...my view of a tank is to deal good damage and take a LOT of damage.<BR>For that, you will need AC and HP.<P>in order of priority:<P>AC is king...there is a rumored soft cap of 1100AC...but more AC is good.<P>STA is probably the next most important...more STA = more HP and also makes them heavy weapons not so bad. Data seems to indicate that STA &gt; 100 is best. From parsed logs, once +100, having zero-fatigue means nothing to your dmg output. <P>STR, is important, but once you got enough STR to carry all your gear and loot, you're pretty much set. I'd shoot for 125-150'ish unbuffed. With most groups, you're going to have a druid, shaman or bard around to buff your STR. If you can boost AC, STA and STR without dropping AC and/or STA...then even better.<P>Haste:<BR>Getting a haste item will definitly help you fullfill the damage taker & dealer role...mostly due to the highier amount of hate you will be able to build from hitting the mob so much faster then anyone else.<P> <BR>Sleethr   posted 06-20-2001 10:07 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Dark Elf Warrior<BR>STR 70 <BR>STA 75 <BR>AGI 90 <BR>DEX 75 <BR>WIS 83 <BR>INT 99 <BR>CHA 60 <BR>Bonus: 25 <BR>Based on physical stats alone, DE Warrior is probably not the "best" choice for a warrior. But, still very doable. AGI is really good, but STR and STA are pretty poor. The Guide is recommending putting all the points into STR, but I think +STR gear is damn easy to get...so I think I would've done +15 STR and +10STA...but tough choice and rather late now anyway.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Not sure what the STA to HP formula is, maybe Ghall can poke some holes in my STA theory.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P> <BR>Nefarius   posted 06-20-2001 10:13 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Well from what I've learned though the wonderful world of power leveling is, AC helps the most. With STA being next. When I started doing my twinking I went for AC and STR, when I should have gone AC and STA. Then to add to my delima I got a FBSS and now I never have anything in the yellow bar.<BR>I'll have to aggree with Sleethr, go with AC and STA. Try to get your STR somewhere around 125+. And as for haste, all it did for me was make me notice how much more I was missing the target.<BR> <BR>Zanath   posted 06-20-2001 10:23 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>My Str is currently at 146, my Sta is at 95, and Agi is at 110. Funny I thought Sta would be a Primary stat. I mean I read it but everyone is so up on getting Str to 200 I never thought of getting Sta. <BR>I have Crustacean Shell Boots +12 Sta and a Dusty BP 22ac +5 Sta. I will hit eqprices when I get home and try to find some good AC/STA Items that I can get. I know two Items I have that are still poor that I can work on are Bronze Arms, and Leather Cape so I will check there first, Also got Crafted Gauntlets which pretty much suck that I will look to upgrading with STA.<P>Thanks for the advice you 2 I knew you could help.<P> <BR>Sleethr   posted 06-20-2001 10:43 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Well...the Wurm/Stamina Slayer, while a nice weapon doesn't really help your STA much.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><BR>I'd also look for some light high damage & low delay weapons. Myself, I'd get that BEFORE a FBBS or haste item.<P>The lighter the weapon, the less fatigue you lose<P>The lower the delay...the more dmg you end up doing. You may not see all them 150+ crits like you can get from a WS, but you will see a ton more hits that more then make up for it. Lower delay also will help you taunt better.<P>Try finding a pair of these babies. Drops in Sebilis so may not be that hard to get if you can get in on a rett/jugg raid and win the roll.<P> <P> <P>sorry..no prices listed, but guessing...10-20K...if you can find one for sale.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P> <BR>Sleethr   posted 06-20-2001 10:45 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR> <BR>see if this one works...if not...it's the:<P>Blade of the Green Dragon Eye<P> <BR>Lonar   posted 06-20-2001 10:59 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Blade of the Black Dragon Eye no longer drops there, if it still drops at all its in VPeak, if I recall correctly. The other one is also exceedingly rare. Of all the juggy/reet/myconid raids i've been on, I've only ever seen one drop. Damn nice weapon if you can manage to get one, but I wouldn't hold my breath.<BR>Sendil/Lonar<BR> <BR>Nefarius   posted 06-20-2001 12:31 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Damn it, now you ruined my wet dreams. <BR>Sleethr   posted 06-20-2001 01:01 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Mine too...I can't believe VI would remove/move an item without telling me! :-)<P>--------------------<P>Sleethr Dragynthorn
